# Text is stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform. Scripts, units and configs are embedded into the program
# with include_str! and run on the NAS (busybox / dash), where a "\r" breaks them ("Syntax error: word unexpected (expecting
# "do")"); the Windows release build checked them out with CRLF. The program also strips "\r" when it embeds them
# (payload::lf), this keeps the working tree clean too.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.xz binary
*.pdf binary
*.msi binary
*.exe binary
*.dtb binary
*.bin binary
